---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { route } from '../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/seo';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL } from '../data/site-config';
const lang = 'en';
const updated = '2026-10-05';
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy Policy of PlantCare101: Analytics, Data and Rights" description="Privacy policy of PlantCare101: calculator inputs stay in your browser, Clarity and Google Analytics measure visits, legal basis, retention and your rights." lang={lang} noindex={true} jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', path: route('privacy', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Privacy policy</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang="en" />
    <h2>What the tools do not collect</h2>
    <p>The tools run entirely in your browser. The plant, pot size, light, season and other values you enter, and the plant names you search in the pet-safe checker, are not sent to our servers and are not stored anywhere; in Microsoft Clarity recordings, what you type is masked. There is no account, no newsletter and no form. If you use the share link of the watering calculator, your inputs are written into the page address: only the people you send it to can see them, but the address of a page opened from that link is recorded by the audience measurement described below.</p>
    <h2>Hosting logs</h2>
    <p>The site is hosted by {LEGAL.hosting.name}. Like any web server, the host records technical data for each request, such as the IP address, the page requested, the date and the browser type, to deliver the site and protect it against abuse. Legal basis: legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). We do not use these logs to identify visitors.</p>
    <h2>Audience measurement: Microsoft Clarity</h2>
    <p>Microsoft Clarity (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited) loads as soon as a page opens, with no consent banner. It produces session recordings and heatmaps: clicks, scrolling, pages viewed and their address, device and browser type, and an approximate location derived from the IP address. Purpose: understanding which plant guides and tools are useful and where readers get stuck. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in understanding how the site is used (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Cookies: <code>_clck</code> (one year), <code>_clsk</code> (one day), and possibly <code>MUID</code> and <code>CLID</code> on Microsoft domains. Retention: 30 days for recordings, up to 13 months for aggregated statistics.</p>
    <h2>Audience measurement: Google Analytics 4</h2>
    <p>Google Analytics 4 (Google Ireland Limited) loads the same way, without a banner. It records pages viewed, where the visit came from, its duration and engagement, the device type and an approximate location (country, city); the IP address is not stored. Purpose and legal basis: as for Clarity (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Cookies: <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_E9EV1P52L4</code>, two years. Retention: 14 months.</p>
    <h2>How to object</h2>
    <p>Block third-party cookies or the clarity.ms and google-analytics.com domains in your browser, or install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>. The site stays fully usable. Cookie details are on the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a>. The site shows no advertising.</p>
    <h2>Recipients and processors</h2>
    <p>No data is sold, rented or shared for advertising. The following act as processors under Article 28 GDPR: the host, {LEGAL.hosting.name}; Microsoft (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited and Microsoft Corporation) for Clarity; Google (Google Ireland Limited, and Google LLC for transfers) for Google Analytics.</p>
    <h2>Transfers outside the European Union</h2>
    <p>The host, Microsoft Corporation and Google LLC are based in the United States and certified under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework; transfers are also covered by the European Commission’s standard contractual clauses. See <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Microsoft’s privacy statement</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google’s privacy policy</a>. Blocking clarity.ms and google-analytics.com avoids the analytics transfers.</p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Since the publisher is established in the European Union, the General Data Protection Regulation gives you rights of access, correction, erasure, restriction, objection and portability over personal data concerning you. If you write to us, we keep your email only as long as needed to answer. For any request, write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. You may also complain to the French supervisory authority, the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority}.</p>
    <p>Last updated: {updated}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
